{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464076-help-constructing-a-halloween-one-shot","id":1464076,"title":"Help constructing a halloween one-shot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-15T13:36:15-07:00","id":1464076,"title":"Help constructing a halloween one-shot","content":"I\u2019m toying with the idea of running a newbie friendly Halloween one-shot for a group of RP enthusiasts. I\u2019m assuming they have no experience with WoD. I\u2019m not sure what numbers I\u2019ll have, but let\u2019s assume up to 6 players<br /> <br /> The idea in my mind is that they would all be a part of a Verbena coven, getting ready to celebrate Samhain by communing with the dead. However, they get the attention of a spectre who takes this opportunity to ask for aid. I haven\u2019t decided what the spectre would ask for, but it needs to be something that seems innocent enough, but turns out to have disastrous consequences that the Mages then need to fix before things get irreversible.<br /> <br /> To make life easier for them, I would partially pregen their character sheets.<br /> <br /> They would all start with 3 Arete and have access to Life 1 and Spirit 1 right off the bat. I\u2019d tell them they can distribute 4 dots in any of the other spheres up to Arete. I will go over what the spheres do, and give everyone access to single sphere rotes such life sense, touch spirit, and whatever else depending on their selection.<br /> <br /> They can assign dots normally for abilities and attributes, but for time and simplicity sake I won\u2019t bother with backgrounds, and just allow everyone to have 5 points of quintessence from the start. It being a oneshot, most background choices are quite simply not going to come up, and people are really here for the magic anyway.<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t think there\u2019s enough time to focus on avatar communion, and can have them all share the same paradigm that magic is in blood and ritual, and impose classic pagan iconography as their primary instrument. Daggers, cups, coins, staves, blood spilling, chanting, all that good stuff.<br /> <br /> Hopefully it will give them all a nice taste of what Mage is like while being appropriately halloween themed, but also not horrendously overwhelming.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like some help thinking about what the spectre is actually going to try and do. One idea was to bring them to a local chorister priest and try to convince them that the priest was responsible for a number of murders and that for them to \u201cpass on\u201d they need him to die.<br /> <br /> They would need to find the priest and get to him, and possibly do some investigating to see how true the spectre\u2019s claims are. Spoiler alert, they are not. The priest did indeed kill the spectre, but they were embroiled in nephandic demonology, something the priest managed to stop, and sealed a number of demons summoned by the spectre upon their death.<br /> <br /> In any event, once the players get near to the priest, if they try to confront him, the priest would initially act dismissive, and would be hostile if the knives are out, suspecting them of being some nephandic cult. If they subdue and talk to him then the truth comes out.<br /> <br /> If they kill him, then their seal on the demons breaks and they\u2019ll have demons to deal with if they don\u2019t find a way to close it up again.<br /> <br /> If they choose not to kill him, the spectre will try to possess someone and do it themselves.<br /> <br /> Might be a bit too complex though, not sure. Also I might swap out the demons for lovecraft centric things.<br /> <br /> Any feedback would be helpful, especially if you\u2019ve had experience running a newbie friendly one-shot.<br /> <br /> If you think this is too dense, I would like to hear advice on thinning it out.<br /> Also, if you have a completely different suggestion for a good Halloween themed Mage one-shot than what I\u2019ve presented here, I\u2019d love to hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T16:09:33-07:00","id":1464101,"title":"","content":"The first thing I would want to is make it as difficult as possible for the players to verify the specter's claims. Suppose he had a daughter who was left orphaned by his death and he manifests to her in dreams, pleading for her to do this task. She draws pictures of things she sees in her dreams that Specter-Dad is trying to show her. The daughter is in foster care, limiting players' ability to get information from the girl. A school teacher has photocopied the pictures and asked someone in the Cabal to help interpret the images. An advantage of this scenario is that the girl might fear the priest as a result of the specter's own fear of him being projected through the dream. <br /> <br /> Or, if you are *dead set* on it being the players who summon a specter, there a couple of options:<br /> <br /> 1) Have the specter and the demon-summoner be two different people. The specter was a pawn of the summoner in life who continues to believe the summoner's claim that the project had altruistic goals. The specter is telling the truth, from his perspective.<br /> <br /> 2) The specter is a Mage who avoided death by fleeing to the deep umbra. The Magick used by the Chorus Mage put the Infernalist out of commission long enough that he failed to return to Earth before falling to Disembodiment (an RAW thing I don't use). When summoned, he is easily mistaken for a ghost. The players' summoning ritual allows the Infernalist to stay in the room as he gradually Reintegrates. <br /> <br /> 3) Combine #1 and #2. They summon the Disembodied Infernalist who summons his Duped Acolyte. <br /> <br /> To make it hard for the priest to prove his innocence, have something that he knows be the result of someone telling him in a Confession. If the priest reveals the whole truth, he breaks his sacred oath. Give him the Magical Prohibition Flaw. He must gain permission from the confessor to avoid some awful, punitive curse. It becomes even more interesting if the confessor is the Duped Acolyte.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:48:24-07:00","id":1464133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464076-help-constructing-a-halloween-one-shot?p=1464101#post1464101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing I would want to is make it as difficult as possible for the players to verify the specter's claims. Suppose he had a daughter who was left orphaned by his death and he manifests to her in dreams, pleading for her to do this task. She draws pictures of things she sees in her dreams that Specter-Dad is trying to show her. The daughter is in foster care, limiting players' ability to get information from the girl. A school teacher has photocopied the pictures and asked someone in the Cabal to help interpret the images. An advantage of this scenario is that the girl might fear the priest as a result of the specter's own fear of him being projected through the dream. <br /> <br /> Or, if you are *dead set* on it being the players who summon a specter, there a couple of options:<br /> <br /> 1) Have the specter and the demon-summoner be two different people. The specter was a pawn of the summoner in life who continues to believe the summoner's claim that the project had altruistic goals. The specter is telling the truth, from his perspective.<br /> <br /> 2) The specter is a Mage who avoided death by fleeing to the deep umbra. The Magick used by the Chorus Mage put the Infernalist out of commission long enough that he failed to return to Earth before falling to Disembodiment (an RAW thing I don't use). When summoned, he is easily mistaken for a ghost. The players' summoning ritual allows the Infernalist to stay in the room as he gradually Reintegrates. <br /> <br /> 3) Combine #1 and #2. They summon the Disembodied Infernalist who summons his Duped Acolyte. <br /> <br /> To make it hard for the priest to prove his innocence, have something that he knows be the result of someone telling him in a Confession. If the priest reveals the whole truth, he breaks his sacred oath. Give him the Magical Prohibition Flaw. He must gain permission from the confessor to avoid some awful, punitive curse. It becomes even more interesting if the confessor is the Duped Acolyte.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of making the wraith they contact innocent.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the acolyte and the master were killed by the priest who now has an active effect in place to keep the seal in place. The acolyte wants the priest out to justice, while the master, who is full spectre, will watch and subtly mislead them, thwarting their attempt to investigate or learn anything, and if they somehow fail to get the priest killed then they show up with all their spectre abilities to get the job done themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}